Rule 1 (input and weight must share the same floating dtype to avoid unsupported type promotion)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8) ∧ dtype_(v_2) = dtype_(v_1)
>>
Rule 2 (weight must be a Tensor and either scalar (0-D) or 1-D)
{v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_2) = 0 ∨ ndim(v_2) = 1
>>
Rule 3 (when input has at least 2 dims and weight is 1-D, weight length must equal channel size)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_2) ≠ 1 ∨ ndim(v_1) < 2 ∨ shape(v_2, 0) = shape(v_1, 1)
>>
Rule 4 (when input has fewer than 2 dims and weight is 1-D, weight length must be 1)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_2) ≠ 1 ∨ ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∨ shape(v_2, 0) = 1
